{"name":"Pulp","hex":"#e18289","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pulp","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft, moist, shapeless mass or matter.\nA mixture of wood, cellulose and/or rags and water ground up to make paper.\nA mass of chemically processed wood fibres (cellulose).\nA suspension of mineral particles, typically achieved by some form of agitation.\nThe soft center of a fruit.","A mixture of wood, cellulose and/or rags and water ground up to make paper."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or be made into pulp.","To beat to a pulp."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pulp"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fruit","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a fruit is the seed-bearing structure in flowering plants (angiosperms) that is formed from the ovary after flowering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Fruit_Platter-_Seasonal_Fruits.jpg/330px-Fruit_Platter-_Seasonal_Fruits.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit"},{"title":"Pulp (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Pulp are an English rock band formed in Sheffield in 1978. At their critical and commercial peak, the band consisted of Jarvis Cocker, Russell Senior, Candida Doyle (keyboards), Nick Banks, Steve Mackey (bass) and Mark Webber. The band's \"kitchen sink drama\" lyrics, coupled with its references to British culture, led to Cocker and Pulp becoming reluctant figureheads of the Britpop movement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/PulpEventim290723_%28110_of_130%29_%2853082647673%29.jpg/330px-PulpEventim290723_%28110_of_130%29_%2853082647673%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pulp_(band)"},{"title":"Pulp (paper)","blocks":[{"text":"Pulp is a fibrous lignocellulosic material prepared by chemically, semi-chemically, or mechanically isolating the cellulosic fibers of wood, fiber crops, waste paper, or rags. Mixed with water and other chemicals or plant-based additives, pulp is the major raw material used in papermaking and the industrial production of other paper products."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Zellstoff_200_fach_Polfilter.jpg/330px-Zellstoff_200_fach_Polfilter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pulp_(paper)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/FruitArrangement.jpg/500px-FruitArrangement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/FruitArrangement.jpg/1280px-FruitArrangement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/FruitArrangement.jpg/500px-FruitArrangement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An arrangement of fruits commonly thought of as culinary vegetables, including maize, tomatoes, and squashes ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFruitArrangement.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Fresh_Fruit_Plate.jpg/500px-Fresh_Fruit_Plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Fresh_Fruit_Plate.jpg/1280px-Fresh_Fruit_Plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Fresh_Fruit_Plate.jpg/500px-Fresh_Fruit_Plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresh fruit plate","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFresh_Fruit_Plate.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Fig_cut_open.jpg/500px-Fig_cut_open.jpg?utm_sour